<Learn
  title="India Atlas — Learn · Revisions: the number will change"
  description="Learn № 14 — GDP is estimated, re-estimated and finalised over about three years, while CPI is final on release and never revised. Why early prints lean on listed companies and government accounts, and how to treat a first print as a pencil sketch, not a photograph."
  slug="revisions"
  kicker="Learn № 14 — Reading numbers · Revisions"
  h1="Every first print is a <i>pencil sketch.</i>"
  lede="GDP is published before the evidence has finished arriving, and then corrected as it arrives, for about three years. The inflation rate, by contrast, is final the day it comes out. Two numbers, two opposite rules, and one habit that serves for both: ask which edition you are reading."
  meta={[
